        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Oriskany</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">6 August 1777</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">A marshy ravine about 6 miles (10 km) east of Fort Stanwix, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oneida-people">Oneida</a> village of Oriska, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohawk-people">Mohawk</a> Valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">Tryon County militia, about 800 men, and between 60 and 100 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oneida-people">Oneida</a> warriors under Brigadier General Nicholas Herkimer; against a force of roughly 500 under Lieutenant Colonel Sir John Johnson, mostly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohawk-people">Mohawk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seneca-people">Seneca</a>, Cayuga, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onondaga-people">Onondaga</a> and Mississauga warriors led by Sayenqueraghta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornplanter">Cornplanter</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-brant">Joseph Brant</a>, with Royal Yorkers and Indian Department rangers</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Americans lost around 465 dead, wounded or captured and Johnson's force 93; the relief column was stopped and Herkimer was mortally wounded, but a sortie from Fort Stanwix looted the warriors' camps and the fighting broke off.</span></div>
