    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Americans suffered around 465 dead, wounded or captured, against 93 for Johnson's force; about half of Herkimer's men were killed or wounded.</li><li>The ambush was sprung too early, and a sortie from Fort Stanwix looted the Indigenous camps, which led the warriors to break off the fight to protect their women and possessions.</li><li>The battle began a civil war among the Haudenosaunee, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oneida-people">Oneida</a> and Tuscarora warriors sided with the Patriots and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohawk-people">Mohawk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seneca-people">Seneca</a>, Cayuga and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onondaga-people">Onondaga</a> with the Loyalist cause.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Many of the men who fought each other at Oriskany had been neighbours, and the Royal Yorkers' ruse of turning their coats inside out to pass as a relief party from the fort failed when a Patriot captain recognised a Loyalist neighbour.</p></aside>
    </section>

